# =============================================================================
# Docker build-context exclusions for the two images built from the REPOSITORY
# ROOT: spaces/api/Dockerfile (the API, same image the Hugging Face Space runs)
# and Dockerfile.web (the local/self-hosted frontend).
#
# The satellite image is NOT built from here: it has its own Dockerfile and
# .dockerignore under satellite-ml/, and compose builds it with satellite-ml/ as
# the context. That whole tree is therefore excluded below — neither root image
# reads a byte of it.
#
# The Space repo assembled by spaces/api/sync.sh carries its own, narrower
# .dockerignore (spaces/api/space.dockerignore); keep the two in agreement about
# what must never enter an image layer.
#
# Strategy: exclude-list. Everything not listed here is shipped to the daemon,
# so newly added source directories work without touching this file.
# =============================================================================

# --- VCS / editor / OS -------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
*.swp

# Claude Code worktrees hold a FULL second copy of the repo — never ship it.
.claude

# --- Node / Next.js ----------------------------------------------------------
# node_modules is reinstalled from package-lock.json inside the image, and
# .next / out are rebuilt. Shipping them makes the context ~10x larger and can
# poison the build with host-arch native modules.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
out
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info
.venv
**/.venv
venv
**/venv
# ml-service/agrotech is a checked-out virtualenv (agrotech/lib/python3.14/...),
# NOT the Python package. The package lives in ml-service/src/agrotech_ml.
ml-service/agrotech
ml-service/catboost_info

# --- Runtime state -----------------------------------------------------------
# ml-service/artifacts is deliberately NOT excluded: the API image bakes the
# trained models (~170 MB) so a cold-started container answers immediately
# instead of re-training. A clean checkout has only .gitkeep there, and the
# build still succeeds — the service trains on first boot instead.
#
# What must never enter a layer, from that directory or anywhere else:
#   * agrotech.db — farmer PII
#   * user uploads — user-submitted files
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
ml-service/uploads

# The satellite module builds from its own context (satellite-ml/Dockerfile with
# satellite-ml/.dockerignore), so none of it belongs in the api/web context.
satellite-ml

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Never bake credentials into a layer. They arrive at runtime as Space secrets,
# Vercel env vars or compose env. Docker matches .dockerignore patterns against
# the FULL relative path, so a bare `.env` would only cover the repo root —
# `**/` is required to also catch ml-service/.env, which exists on dev machines
# and holds a real API key. (.env.example files are kept — they are docs.)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*-service-account*.json
**/*-sa-key*.json
**/credentials.json

# --- Docs / tooling that no image needs --------------------------------------
docs
scripts/sqlite_to_postgres.py
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
README.md
spaces/api/DEPLOY.md
spaces/api/sync.sh
